The rebase-durable half of the staleness gate's clearing rule — design #415 D7,
job #482. `.chug/tasks/doc-staleness.sh --gate` blocks a doc this diff edits that
is still suspect through a non-doc file it names, and clears it on an asserted
re-read: a `Doc-reread: <path>` line, one per doc, either as a trailer in a
commit message on your branch or as a line added to this file. Only the second
survives a rebase — a rework that squashes or re-authors your commits takes a
commit message with it.

THIS IS A SCRATCH SLATE, NOT A REGISTRY. The gate reads the lines your diff ADDS
against its base, never the file's contents, so every line below is inert the
moment it merges and asserts nothing about any later branch. Nothing prunes it
and nothing has to; rewrite it wholesale if you need it.

